  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 144 AM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nA pattern change could be on the way as Wednesday's setup is similar \nto Tuesday with another round of storms off the mountains expected \nto track across the Panhandles.  Thursday we'll have to watch a bit \ncloser, as there is conflicting models.  It may yet again be like \nanther Tuesday and Wednesday, but there is a hint that the ridge may \nshift a bit further west giving us more of a northerly flow and the \nstorms could stay off to the west in NM.\n\nFriday through Sunday the ridge tries to shift further west \nincluding over the Panhandles by Sunday and with that comes the hot \ntemperature return and limited precipitation chances. \n\nWeber",
